"## Flow: 5226\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/flows/5226\n- **Name**: Export reporting data\n- **Screens Count**: 4\n- **Description**: Happy path: a signed-in user on the Reporting overview opens the Download report modal to export raw data. The modal lets the user choose a date range, pick the basis for the report (e.g., expense date), add optional filters, and select which columns to include. After selecting columns the user triggers either an Excel or CSV download. Entry point is the Reporting screen’s \"Download report\" control (top-right). Exit point is the system starting report generation and providing the chosen file for download. Assumptions: user is authenticated and on a desktop/larger screen where the modal displays over the dashboard.\n- **Problem**: User goal: export a custom dataset from the Reporting dashboard so they can analyze or share travel/expense/trip records. From the user perspective they expect to: pick a time range, choose the date basis, optionally filter the dataset, hand-pick data columns to include, and get a downloadable CSV or Excel file that matches those selections. From the interface perspective the UI: provides controls for date range and basis, an Add filter action, a searchable/organized list of report column checkboxes (grouped by category), a live counter of selected columns, and explicit Download actions for CSV or Excel. Result: user-perceived outcome — a file that contains the selected columns and date scope; system-level outcome — the platform packages the selected data into the requested file format and makes it available for download (the modal shows generation/progress feedback while preparing the file).\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 623\n- **Name**: TravelPerk \n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/623\n- **Domain**: travelperk.com\n- **Categories**: Productivity, Travel & Booking\n- **Description**: Book your next business trip\n\n### Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Reporting overview\n- **Screen ID**: 456e1768-0341-4356-83dd-3b7c8ecbec6e\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/456e1768-0341-4356-83dd-3b7c8ecbec6e\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/travelperk.com/desktop/5b61cb6f-a47b-4270-9a1b-0e10ad315f3d_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Access export functionality for the account's travel reporting data\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Download report\" button in the top-right of the Reporting screen\n- **System Response**: A modal dialog titled \"Download report\" opens on top of the dashboard, revealing export controls (date range, basis, filters) and the \"Select report columns\" area with checkboxes.\n- **Page Types**: Dashboard\n- **UX Patterns**: Empty State, Stats\n- **UI Elements**: Cards & Tiles, Button, Navigation Bar, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: \n- **Content**\n  - Description: A corporate travel reporting dashboard on a light beige background with a minimalist top nav, a large Reporting title, date-range controls, black action buttons, and stacked analytics cards showing zeroed travel, spend, CO₂, sustainability, and credit metrics, plus an AI prompt banner at the bottom.\n  - Layout: Single-column vertical dashboard with a full-width top navigation bar, a heading and inline controls beneath it, then multiple wide rounded stat cards stacked with generous spacing and subtle shadows.\n  - Functions: Lets users filter reporting by date range, review key travel and sustainability metrics, open full report sections, download reports, and use Ask AI for quick insights.\n\n#### Step 2: Download report — initial column selection\n- **Screen ID**: 8b5444e0-c12d-4e01-8ebb-1a1ad93039f4\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/8b5444e0-c12d-4e01-8ebb-1a1ad93039f4\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/travelperk.com/desktop/cdc2ea2a-a5c4-4c42-90bc-2d23f29b9bd7_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Review default column selection and report scope before exporting\n- **Action**: User reviews or changes Date range and \"Based on\" options, optionally clicks \"Add filter\", and inspects the pre-checked columns in the Select report columns list\n- **System Response**: The UI shows the current selection count (e.g., 80/80 selected). All chosen columns are checked and ready. Download buttons for Excel and CSV are available.\n- **UX Patterns**: Upload & Download\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Checkbox & Radio, Side Sheet\n- **Fonts**: \n- **Content**\n  - Description: A centered “Download report” modal overlays a travel reporting dashboard, letting users configure export settings with dropdowns, filters, and checkbox column groups before downloading as Excel or CSV.\n  - Layout: A single-column modal form with a title bar, two top dropdowns, an Add filter button, grouped checkbox sections, and bottom-right download actions, over a dimmed dashboard background.\n  - Functions: Users can customize a travel report export by choosing date range, data basis, optional filters, and which columns to include, then download the result as Excel or CSV.\n\n#### Step 3: Download report — customize columns\n- **Screen ID**: f44b1d5d-982b-4ae7-aa79-23160b275aee\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/f44b1d5d-982b-4ae7-aa79-23160b275aee\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/travelperk.com/desktop/e61ac789-3972-432f-bd99-20c5a83f8544_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Reduce or customize which fields will appear in the exported file\n- **Action**: User checks or unchecks individual column group items (traveller info, trip info, service info, expense info). The selected count updates (for example to 64/80).\n- **System Response**: Checkbox states update immediately and the selected columns counter reflects the change. Download controls remain enabled so the user can proceed when ready.\n- **UX Patterns**: Upload & Download\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Checkbox & Radio, Side Sheet\n- **Fonts**: \n- **Content**\n  - Description: A Travelperk reporting dashboard is dimmed behind a centered \"Download report\" modal with date range and basis dropdowns, an \"Add filter +\" button, grouped column checkboxes, and footer buttons to download Excel or CSV.\n  - Layout: Centered white modal over a gray-dimmed dashboard; header with title and close icon, two side-by-side dropdown filters, an add-filter button, scrollable grouped checklist, and right-aligned download buttons at the bottom.\n  - Functions: The modal lets users customize a report by choosing date range, report basis, extra filters, and which columns to include, then export the report as Excel or CSV.\n\n#### Step 4: Download report — start generation\n- **Screen ID**: 20be9008-c9eb-4dfb-9e39-12eed664472a\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/20be9008-c9eb-4dfb-9e39-12eed664472a\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/travelperk.com/desktop/e20f04bc-c971-4368-b0f5-3da7f2a44653_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Start creating the export file with the chosen settings\n- **Action**: User clicks a download action (Download CSV or Download Excel).\n- **System Response**: The modal shows a processing state (controls disabled/greyed and a spinner or progress indicator). The interface indicates report generation is in progress and will provide the file for download when ready.\n- **UX Patterns**: Loading & Connecting, Upload & Download\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Dropdown, Checkbox & Radio, Side Sheet\n- **Fonts**: \n- **Content**\n  - Description: A centered modal titled “Download report” overlays a dimmed reporting dashboard, letting users choose date range, basis, filters, and report columns before exporting CSV.\n  - Layout: Centered modal over a blurred dashboard, with top filter dropdowns, grouped checkbox columns in the middle, and a footer containing info text, spinner, and Download CSV button.\n  - Functions: Used to configure and export a custom report by selecting date range, basis, filters, and included columns, then downloading the result as a CSV.\n\n### Related Queries\n- download report modal columns\n- export reporting date range selection\n- report columns checkbox export\n- generate CSV export reporting\n- select report fields export\n- reporting download dialog flow\n- report export based on expense date\n- filter and export reporting data\n- report generation progress modal\n- choose columns download Excel"
